    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d705">

                <pb facs="0935" n="821" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg821"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">550.E1 Russia/59: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sussdorff</hi>)<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d705-f1"/></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-07-15T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 15, 1922—2
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>49. Legation’s No. 65 of July 14, 5 p.m. Inform Mr. Cattier, and if you think
                    best the other chief delegates also, that this Government gives no countenance
                    to any arrangements with the authorities of Soviet Russia by American citizens
                    that would jeopardize or prejudice vested rights in Soviet Russia held by the
                    nationals of other countries and that the American Government is fully confident
                    that the same policy will be followed by the other interested Governments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d705-f1" n="42" type="source" xml:id="d705-f1-content">
                <p>By telegrams dated July 16, 2 p.m., the substance of this telegram was repeated
                    to the Ambassadors in Belgium, France, and Great Britain, to be conveyed to the
                    respective Foreign Offices.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
